<title>NEW ZEALAND: Progressive details staff option plan.</title>
<headline>Progressive details staff option plan.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Progressive Enterprises Ltd said on Tuesday it had formed a share option plan for its 800 senior and long-serving employees.</p>
<p>The scheme involves about 4.2 million options, exercisable at NZ$1.42 over periods starting October 1999 and expiring in December, 2002. Shares in the supermarket operator last traded at NZ$1.50.</p>
<p>Progressive also proposed to offer 750,000 options on identical terms to managing director Graeme Kelly, subject to shareholder approval. The board said aligning the interests of employees and shareholders would encourage long-term commitment  </p>
<p>to the group.</p>
<p>Progressive is majority owned by Australia's Foodland Associated Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
</text>
